    <item>
      <title>TravelMedallion10X</title>
      <author>Ylimhs</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/745645</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/745645#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7bb686d9bbc85f36c51782b1e8e1303fd1e310e8</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:29:42 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b074dc29bf83.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b075306aec55.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b075305e8707.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;# Travel Medallion 10&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep up to ten fast-travel destinations with the Travel Medallion in *The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild*. Each destination saves its own position and facing direction. The mod works on the original map as a standalone install.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## How to use&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. In **Key Items**, select the Travel Medallion and choose **Place** to use an available slot.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Select a Travel Medallion marker on the map and choose **Travel**, **Delete**, or **Cancel**. Deleting a marker frees its slot and leaves the other destinations in place.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Once all ten slots are full, delete a marker on the map before placing another. A placement attempt at capacity preserves all ten destinations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your existing destination from the original game moves into the first slot on first use. Saves already using Travel Medallion 10 retain their destinations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The custom full-capacity message is available in Simplified Chinese (CNzh). Other languages use the game's existing wording.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Requirements&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Nintendo Switch edition of *Breath of the Wild* updated to **1.9.0**, with game executable Build ID `CD57B23FA4BBAD65803D9788C01821EE00000000000000000000000000000000`.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Atmosphère for the included Switch installation layout.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Expansion Pass DLC installed and the Travel Medallion already obtained in your save.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Install on Switch&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Close the game completely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Extract `TravelMedallion10-1.9.0-NS.zip` and copy its `atmosphere` folder to the root of your SD card. Merge it with the existing `atmosphere` folder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Start the game and load your save.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To use this mod with **Main Field Outer Ring**, install `MainFieldOuterRing+TravelMedallion10-1.9.0-NS.zip`. This compatibility package includes the merged resource size table (RSTB) required by both mods. Other mods that change `Bootup.pack`, `Bootup_CNzh.pack`, or the RSTB need a resource merge.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Testing&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Placement, deletion, the ten-slot limit, map travel, and save persistence were verified in SavageWindRecomp on PC. Gameplay verification on Switch hardware and emulators is pending.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;switch botw 1.9.0：✔&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/travelmedallion10-190-ns.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Player</category>
      <category>Game files</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>MainFieldOuterRing Ex</title>
      <author>Ylimhs</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/745638</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/745638#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">98ade747395ddd5560bb0697323722d35b9556df</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:50:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b073a076fbf5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b073a3c5583f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;# Main Field Outer Ring&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Explore an extra kilometer of Hyrule in every direction in *The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild*. Main Field Outer Ring adds 40 playable chunks around the original 80, bringing the overworld to 120 chunks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The game streams each new chunk through its ordinary map system, with its own object placement, decoration resources, and terrain collision. The original 80 chunk names and coordinates stay the same.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The playable boundary moves outward to X ±6,000 m and Z ±5,000 m, with boundary winds starting 80 m inside the new edge. The map cursor and panning reach the expanded area.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The outer ring has four climates. The north is cooler, the south is warm and wet, the west is dry, and the east is mild.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The new areas are for terrain exploration, with no new NPCs, quests, or NPC navigation meshes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Walk past the former world boundary to reach the new terrain. For example, B-9 is south of the Gerudo region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Install on Switch&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Requires the Nintendo Switch release of *Breath of the Wild* with update **1.9.0**, Atmosphère, and main executable Build ID `CD57B23FA4BBAD65803D9788C01821EE00000000000000000000000000000000`.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If upgrading from an earlier release, replace its map IPS and map resources together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Close the game and extract `MainFieldOuterRing-1.9.0-NS.zip`.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Copy the included `atmosphere` folder to the root of your SD card.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Restart the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Compatibility&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Install `MainFieldOuterRing+TravelMedallion10-1.9.0-NS.zip` when using both mods. The combined package merges their Resource Size Table (RSTB) entries. Installing the standalone packages over each other overwrites that shared table.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Other mods that replace the same map archives, ActorInfo, or RSTB need their resources merged. The included `manifest.json` lists this package's resource overrides. Save inside the original map before removing the expansion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Testing&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;SavageWindRecomp √&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;eden &amp;nbsp;√&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;switch &amp;nbsp;√&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;UKMM &amp;nbsp;√&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/mainfieldouterring_ex40.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>OverWorld/Field</category>
      <category>Maps</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Girly Animation Pack</title>
      <author>i2m</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/735317</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/735317#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">fce8804905b0b1730db3c756299a00009d8d2213</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:33:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae7d70fce66c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae7d2c706b31.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae7d28f4f006.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Reminder&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;Please note this is the official and latest version of the Girly Animation Pack port for Switch.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class="GreyColor"&gt;In the past, other modders made their port of certain versions of my original mod on WiiU, and I would like to thank them for their work and effort; just right now all are outdated and not maintained anymore. Thanks you all.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/bitpit/gap_00.gif"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/bitpit/gap_info_c2.png"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;This is an experimental &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;u&gt;vive coded&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt; port for Switch of my latest &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49763"&gt;Girly Animation Pack v10.9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;for WiiU. &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;I used &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Codex&lt;/span&gt; for the entire process and then tested the results against BOTW running in the latest Eden emulator. So far, so good.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everything is working as expected: walk, run, sit, talk, jump, sprint, idles... including the extras and bonus options. For a comprehensive list of features, details, options, questions &amp;amp; answers please look at &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49763"&gt;my main mod page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;DISCLAIMER: &lt;/span&gt;I'm offering this port AS-IS. Meaning I may not actively fix it if bugs are found, because this is just an experiment that ended working really good (and I'm not into modding the game anymore --no time, other vital projects, etc--).&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/bitpit/gap_info_c3.png"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;What's all of this?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;I have ZERO experience on Switch and ZERO time to learn it (all my knowledge is on WiiU) and worst, I'm already out of modding the game but... (there's always a "but") ...lately I have been trying crazy things using Codex, and suddenly the idea came to me: why not try to port the most complex mod of mine, to Switch?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;How did you do it?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;In about 20 minutes, plus tests on the Eden emulator. Want to try? Pick a mod. Install Codex from OpenAI on your Windows. Create an empty folder and put there that mod (the BNP file, and the ZIP if available). Then on the Codex app start a new project, attach to it that folder, and start a new chat. On that chat, tell Codex something like that: "&lt;i&gt;Check the BOTW mod file in your working folder, I downloaded it from --the url--&amp;nbsp;&lt;put the="" gamebanana="" url=""&gt;and it's for WiiU but I want you to convert it to Switch making a new BNP file. Download any tool you may need on the working folder but try to use portable editions when possible to avoid installing things on my machine.&lt;/put&gt;&lt;/i&gt;" I used GPT 6.1 Sol on Medium, waited few minutes, and voilà! Not everything was fine, but simply attach screenshots to the chat and tell Codex what's happening and ask to fix it. Let it do the magic. Be Aladdin. Codex can joke too! And you can ask to many times as remaining % on your daily/weekly usage (depending if you're paying Codex or not... I'm a Plus user --20$ monthly-- and it barely used about 25% of a daily usage). You can use &lt;b&gt;Claude&lt;/b&gt;, or any other AI capable of working on your computer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Can I do it?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Of course. You don't have any mods? Be my guess: pick any of my WiiU mods, convert it, play with it. If you like the results and want to share them, do it. Just credit me as the original author and link to the WiiU mod page. No need to ask or anything, just tell me if possible as I would like to know :-) If you do it with other mods not mine not yours, just ask the author(s) before publishing anything, as usual.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;What else?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is just the beginning. Remember that old mod that never got an update? Ask for it. That other mod with problems with the textures? Ask to fix it. That face replacement getting ugly shadows? Let Codex download Blender and FIX IT FOR YOU. Conflicting mods? Merge them! Wondering if a mod can be ported to TOTK? Boldly go for it and see what happens. So... just play with it. Bring your ideas to live, or try them at least. For the first time in forever, you have a full experienced modder at your service. Let it go!&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src="https://files.gamebanana.com/bitpit/gap_install_c.png"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod brings a big overhaul over Link’s more common animations: idles, walk, run, talk… a hundred of animations have been replaced in order to give to a female player, a more girly appearance, as seen in most of the female NPC in the game. Several styles for each replacement are available to mix and get an almost unique style for your gameplay. See the &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49763"&gt;original mod page&lt;/a&gt; for more info and the &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49763"&gt;illustrated list of all the options&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;To install it, don't use the 1-click install option!&lt;br&gt;Please do this:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;If you are upgrading or reinstalling the mod, uninstall it first.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Download the BNP in a folder&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;install it on BCML/UKMM&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;During the setup, a window with options will appear:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Ensure you check &lt;u&gt;one option on each section&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Suggested ones are marked with an asterisk.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Install if &lt;u&gt;AFTER&lt;/u&gt; your replacement mod (Linkle, Zelda…).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If&amp;nbsp; you're using UKMM don't use cached mod and instead use&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; the original files. Avoid symlinks if possible too.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/girly_animation_pack_v109_beta.bnp" type="application/octet-stream"/>
      <category>Player</category>
      <category>Game files</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Hey, Listen! Navi in BotW (Switch)</title>
      <author>zapiltar</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/743088</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/743088#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">841c10139e973fd01649cfc5d6e0698b8a76382a</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:57:45 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6affd712a4ae3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6affd712b6b3a.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6affd712b6d3f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; TotK Edition Parity&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Added feature/behavior parity with the 1.0 TotK mod release&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Hey, Listen!&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod brings Navi, the Hero of Time's trusty companion to Breath of the Wild!&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Navi takes over the game's ZL targeting, both the soft lock white arrow, and the hard lock orange arrow. When you target a hostile npc she glows orange, targeting a friendly npc she glows green.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When you aren't in combat or chatting with people, she floats over Link's left shoulder occasionally chattering. If Link stands around long enough Navi will get bored and start flying around in the vicinity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;During cutscenes or dialog, Navi hides in Link's hat/hair until the player regains control of Link; this is to avoid any odd behavior and maintain some continuity with her missing in prerendered cutscenes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She will also hide when Link freefalls, rides a horse, and during fast travel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Installation Guide&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Emulators&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Ryujinx/Ryubing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Right click BOTW &amp;gt; Open Mods Directory&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy Navi folder from the zip's Emulator folder into the opened directory&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Eden/Yuzu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Right click BOTW &amp;gt; Open Mod Data Location&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy Navi folder from the zip's Emulator folder into the opened directory&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Enable Navi in the &lt;i&gt;BOTW&amp;gt;Properties&amp;gt;Add-Ons&lt;/i&gt; menu&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Hardware&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Standalone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Open the zip's Atmosphere folder and copy the atmosphere folder inside it to the root of the sd card.&lt;br&gt;SD:/atmosphere/contents/01007EF00011E000/&amp;nbsp; (romfs + exefs folders inside) is the final filepath.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Mod Merge Tools&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;UKMM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Unzip the _ModManager.zip download&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Point UKMM at the Navi (UKMM).zip and it will install the Navi mod [ Don't unzip &lt;b&gt;Navi (UKMM).zip&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;]&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Hit Deploy, if UKMM doesn't deploy to your SDcard copy the folders to &lt;i&gt;atmosphere/contents&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy the &lt;i&gt;atmosphere &lt;/i&gt;folder from &lt;i&gt;Navi Code/Atmosphere&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;to merge with &lt;i&gt;atmosphere&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;at the SDcard root.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;BCML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Unzip the _ModManager.zip download&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- In BCML, select &lt;i&gt;Navi (BCML)/info.json&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Merge or Remerge&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy the &lt;i&gt;atmosphere &lt;/i&gt;folder from &lt;i&gt;Navi Code/Atmosphere&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;to merge with &lt;i&gt;atmosphere&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;at the SDcard root.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Mod Settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Edit &lt;i&gt;romfs/Navi/settings.txt&lt;/i&gt; to change her volume, language, and chatter frequency, then restart the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Tested&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod was made for and tested on BotW 1.6.0 on the Ryubing emulator and real hardware running firmware 22.1.0, Atmosphere 1.11.2&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;AI Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;Claude Code was used for the reverse engineering and as a programming assistant to understand the game memory and code addresses that are used to hook Navi to each of Link's and the game states, trigger sounds, and change npc states.&lt;h1&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;b&gt;Other Releases&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/742763"&gt;Cemu 1.5.0 Edition&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/744196"&gt;TotK 1.2.1/1.4.3 Edition&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
