    <item>
      <title>Unauthorized Horse (Switch 1.6.0 port)</title>
      <author>akirus10879</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/735044</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/735044#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">ae12340e17bf429cea4db8b6d9629819bf5dedcc</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:20:40 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae73bbc89e54.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae73bbce4fe3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unauthorized Horse (Switch 1.6.0 port)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Lets you summon your horse in areas where it normally can’t be called, such as the Gerudo Desert and Eldin, and stops it despawning in the desert. It works best with the Ancient/warping armor from the DLC.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Credits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This is a port of the Wii U mod &lt;em&gt;Unauthorized Horse&lt;/em&gt; by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class="MemberLink" href="https://gamebanana.com/members/2116184" data-id="member_2116184"&gt;aaron31121&lt;/a&gt;, All credit for the idea and the original research goes to him: [link to gamebanana.com/mods/371538]. His description also thanks Leoetlino for the guide “Patching the motorcycle area checks”, which helped with finding similar code. The Switch patch was made by [your name] with help from Claude (an AI assistant), by matching the Wii U patch’s logic in the Switch 1.6.0 code.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Compatibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul dir="ltr"&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;BotW &lt;strong&gt;1.6.0 only&lt;/strong&gt; (build ID &lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;8E9978D50BDD20B4C8395A106C27FFDE&lt;/code&gt;). It does nothing on other versions.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Tested on &lt;strong&gt;Eden&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;only with the Ancient horse armor equipped&lt;/strong&gt;. It hasn’t been tested without the armor, so a horse called without it may behave differently (for example, it may run to you and get stuck on terrain or an invisible horse wall).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;It has &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; been tested on a real Switch, so use it there at your own risk (stay offline and back up your save).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;It’s a code patch only. It doesn’t change any game files and doesn’t include the original’s removal of invisible horse walls.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Install (Eden / Yuzu-style emulators)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol dir="ltr"&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Right-click BotW and choose &lt;strong&gt;Open Mod Data Location&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Put the &lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;Unauthorized Horse&lt;/code&gt; folder from this download into that folder, so the path ends in &lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;Unauthorized Horse\exefs\UnauthorizedHorse.pchtxt&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Right-click the game, go to &lt;strong&gt;Properties → Add-Ons&lt;/strong&gt;, and tick &lt;strong&gt;Unauthorized Horse&lt;/strong&gt; and the 1.6.0 update.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Install (Atmosphère, real Switch, untested)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Copy the &lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;atmosphere&lt;/code&gt; folder to the root of your SD card, reboot, and launch the game. To remove it, delete &lt;code dir="ltr"&gt;/atmosphere/exefs_patches/UnauthorizedHorse&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/unauthorizedhorse.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Game files</category>
      <category>Game files</category>
    </item>
