    <item>
      <title>Hyrule Rebalance [Switch][ABANDONED]</title>
      <author>Kitsen</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/443023</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/443023#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">719c73f78ca6b87f56c788edf3380041c41c3c44</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:55:33 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c67fd4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c6071f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c6ac5c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c9f4dc.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c73511.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c798c9.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c6cd30.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c9a26e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/645d2a0c51aaa.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; abandoning it&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sadly I'm behind two updates now and I don't see myself having enough time to update it, leaving it to the next guy to do what I couldn't, go YOU!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;[This port is now abandoned officially, if someone wants to take over and update it to the latest version feel free to do so!]&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This a Switch port of Hyrule Rebalanced based on version 7.12.&lt;br&gt;The originally bundled modules of HR will be distributed via seperate bnps during the beta period for easier troubleshooting.&lt;br&gt;The port was made using the &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/tools/7836"&gt;Ultimate BotW Converter&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and then repair what got broken in the process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The dye module wasn't ported by me, instead I will direct you towards&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/403020"&gt;Hyrule Rebalance's Dye for Switch&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1683828"&gt;XModxGodX&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Make sure the main module sits at a lower priority than the other ones to avoid compatilibty issue, &lt;a href="https://imgur.com/p4Ah0Te" target="_blank"&gt;like so&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It's ben extensively tested on switch and yuzu so rest assured that unless I missed something, you should have a good ol' time!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you have any issue make sure to mention as much details as possible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;here's the text included with the&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49532"&gt; Wii U version&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;updated by me&lt;br&gt;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Hyrule Rebalance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;aims to fix BotW's fundamentally unbalanced elements – to&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;tone down&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;its overly dependable mechanics and&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;improve&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;alternatives – in an effort to expand the player's strategy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;—FAQ—&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;Q: Does this work on&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;Wii U&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;console?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A: use the &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/49532"&gt;Wii U Version&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;Q: Does this work with&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;Crafting&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;Project?&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;Linkle&lt;/span&gt;?&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;Survival&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the Wild? Etc?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A: Most likely. Use your common sense when merging mods.&lt;br&gt;For mods that change Link's appearance, you cannot use the Dye module.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor SelectedElement"&gt;My note: from my personal experience, SW and linkle are semi compatible if they have a higher load order than HR. I will develop a patch for SW soonish based on my WiiU patches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;Q: Does this work on&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;normal&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;mode or&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;master&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;mode?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A: Yes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;Q: Do I have to start a&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;new game&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;for this mod to work?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A: No, you can pick it up anytime you want.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;Q: Will I lose anything from&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;uninstalling&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;this mod?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A: New armour upgrades will not carry over to your regular file – the Thunder Helm is not reobtainable in the base game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;Q: Is there a more&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="PurpleColor"&gt;detailed list&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of changes out there?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1l2TUpmdQ44uhPBokAUMxFp7tR4i_om165ncsbARf0VY" target="_blank"&gt;This spreadsheet records some useful information about weapons, materials, armour and enemies.&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;—SUMMARY OF MODIFICATIONS—&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Rebalanced&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;damage&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;taken&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;– armour and enemy power work together to maintain a stable and flatter difficulty curve throughout the game;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Rebalanced&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;loot&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;– enemy health and wildlife health is proportional to the worth of their loot;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Rebalanced&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;weapon&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;attributes&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;– all weapons of a "family" (Soldier, Gerudo, etc.) have equal total damage, and it generally reflects their rarity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Base durability is shown in the item description&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Rebalanced&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;materials and economy&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;– the rarer a material is, the better its properties.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Potency is shown in the item description&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;All armour is&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;fully upgradeable&lt;/u&gt;, and some were given new effects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Upgrade requirements are listed in the armour's description&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Weapons&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;have new traits to differentiate them from one another;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Bows&lt;/u&gt;' power now also reflect their range&amp;nbsp;and rate-of-fire;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;All&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;shields&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;can deal damage when bashing;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;unused Shield Surf Up&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;weapon effect&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;has been enabled. The less valuable Long Throw&amp;nbsp;and Shield Guard Up bonuses were disabled;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Weaker enemies&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;are spiced up slightly –&amp;nbsp;Chuchus&amp;nbsp;split in two when slain, Stals&amp;nbsp;have a chance of being reborn as floating skulls, and Keese and Octoroks can take more than one hit;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Stronger enemies&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;have less health overall, but they are less prone to&amp;nbsp;staggering, which allowed the player to stunlock them.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Elemental enemies&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;take significant damage from the opposite element, instead of suffering instant death;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Charged attacks&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;deal more damage (×1.5 for swords, ×1.2 for spears, ×2 for katanas). Chain attack finishers deal ×1.2 damage;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Pots&lt;/u&gt;, barrels and crates contain a wide variety of materials and weapons;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Roasted materials&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;can now grant brief special effects, as incentive to roast special ingredients;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Complex recipes&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;grant significant healing bonuses, as incentive to cook more difficult meals;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Swim&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;faster, climb in rain more reliably;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To limit overreliance,&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;Remote Bombs&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;have a slightly longer recharge delay, and are less effective on weak enemies, wildlife and tree logs;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Bugs&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;are bigger, to make them easier to spot;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Quest and minigame&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;NPCs&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;hand out balanced rewards, and some completion requirements were altered;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Inns&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;are cheaper and give more extra hearts;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;Old Man&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;on the Great Plateau can give fairies during the game's prologue;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Merchants&lt;/u&gt;' inventories are more plentiful – town merchants sell rare items, and travelling merchants focus on volume;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Chests in the&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;Trial of the Sword&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;hold several pieces of armour to make the trials less treacherous;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Tier 1&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;status effects&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;are more potent. Some effects (Guardian Resist, Shock Resist, Speed Up) are more potent overall;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Weapons&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;no longer rank up&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;(Traveler -&amp;gt; Soldier, etc.) as you progress through the game, to prevent some weapons from becoming completely unobtainable;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Critters and fish&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;were redistributed in each area to ensure none is underrepresented;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;NPCs are more frightened of&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;Tingle&lt;/u&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Beedle&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;carries weapons – his inventory changes depending on the location&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;(OPTIONAL)&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Every armour in the game is&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;dyeable&lt;/u&gt;, with the exception of jewelry&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;(OPTIONAL)&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Stamina&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;regenerates slower and some actions cost more stamina (gliding, claymore spin), whereas others cost less (sprinting, charged attacks)&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;(OPTIONAL)&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Flurry Rush&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;only lets you hit 1-2 times, and the activation window is tighter&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;(OPTIONAL)&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;u&gt;Climates&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;are more varied and temperature damage is replaced with increased stamina cost&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;(OPTIONAL)&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;—KNOWN ISSUES—&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;There is no major&amp;nbsp;issue&amp;nbsp;known currently.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;—INSTALLING—&lt;/h2&gt;Install the modules using BCML individually, make sure the Main module is at le lowest priority than the other ones.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="OrangeColor"&gt;Thank you for trying out the rebalance!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
